{"nodes": [{"id": "docs_src_content_docs_reference_faq_faqpage", "label": "FAQ", "file_type": "document", "source_file": "docs/src/content/docs/reference/faq.mdx", "source_location": "frontmatter", "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Quick answers on API choice, capabilities, runtime compatibility, performance and the frequent 'is this a bug or am I holding it wrong' questions."}, {"id": "docs_src_content_docs_reference_faq_productionreadiness", "label": "Is actor-ts production-ready?", "file_type": "rationale", "source_file": "docs/src/content/docs/reference/faq.mdx", "source_location": "### Is actor-ts production-ready?", "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Pre-1.0: the core actor model is well-tested and stable, cluster features work but expect API polish, and some edges - replicated event sourcing, sharded daemon process variants - are explicitly experimental. Reasonable for a new project shipping before 1.0; budget adoption time for a critical rewrite."}, {"id": "docs_src_content_docs_reference_faq_whyactorts", "label": "Why actor-ts rather than a JVM toolkit or vanilla TS", "file_type": "rationale", "source_file": "docs/src/content/docs/reference/faq.mdx", "source_location": "### Why \"actor-ts\"?", "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "First-class TypeScript types instead of a ported JVM shape, runtime choice (Bun, Node, Deno, no JVM), and cluster plus persistence plus observability built in. If you need none of clustering, persistence or supervision, vanilla Promise code is simpler."}, {"id": "docs_src_content_docs_reference_faq_nobrowsersupport", "label": "It does not work in the browser", "file_type": "rationale", "source_file": "docs/src/content/docs/reference/faq.mdx", "source_location": "### Does it work in the browser?", "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "The framework targets server-side runtimes because most actor patterns - clustering, persistence, TCP transports, file journals - need server-side primitives, and there is no browser-mode build."}, {"id": "docs_src_content_docs_reference_faq_tellaskpipeto", "label": "tell, ask, or pipeTo", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "docs/src/content/docs/reference/faq.mdx", "source_location": "### `tell`, `ask`, or `pipeTo`?", "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "tell is the default fire-and-forget; ask when you need a Promise (HTTP handlers, sagas, tests) but not in tight loops because of the temporary ref; pipeTo when an async result should land as a message instead of awaiting inside onReceive."}, {"id": "docs_src_content_docs_reference_faq_persistentvsdurablestate", "label": "PersistentActor or DurableStateActor", "file_type": "rationale", "source_file": "docs/src/content/docs/reference/faq.mdx", "source_location": "### PersistentActor or DurableStateActor?", "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Pick by whether you need history: PersistentActor persists every state-changing event and replays to recover; DurableStateActor overwrites the current state snapshot."}, {"id": "docs_src_content_docs_reference_faq_singletonshardingdistributeddata", "label": "Singleton, Sharding, or DistributedData", "file_type": "rationale", "source_file": "docs/src/content/docs/reference/faq.mdx", "source_location": "### Singleton, Sharding, or DistributedData?", "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Singleton for exactly one actor cluster-wide, sharding for one actor per key across nodes, DistributedData for eventually-consistent shared state via CRDTs."}, {"id": "docs_src_content_docs_reference_faq_actorscalenumbers", "label": "How many actors can I spawn", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "docs/src/content/docs/reference/faq.mdx", "source_location": "### How many actors can I spawn?", "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Roughly: 100 000 comfortable, 1 000 000 feasible but memory-tight (consider passivation), 10 000 000+ needs sharding across nodes. The dominant cost is the actor's own state, not framework bookkeeping."}, {"id": "docs_src_content_docs_reference_faq_permessageoverhead", "label": "Per-message overhead", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "docs/src/content/docs/reference/faq.mdx", "source_location": "### What's the per-message overhead?", "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "~50 ns and ~200 bytes for tell on the hot path, ~5 us and ~500 bytes for ask, network-bound cross-cluster. Actor messaging costs 50-200x a direct call."}, {"id": "docs_src_content_docs_reference_faq_minimumclustersize", "label": "Minimum cluster size is one node", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "docs/src/content/docs/reference/faq.mdx", "source_location": "### What's the minimum cluster size?", "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Cluster.join with no (or unreachable) seeds gives a singleton cluster whose local node auto-promotes to leader, and every cluster extension works in single-node mode - so cluster code is developable without Docker Compose."}, {"id": "docs_src_content_docs_reference_faq_splitbrainhandling", "label": "How to handle split-brain", "file_type": "rationale", "source_file": "docs/src/content/docs/reference/faq.mdx", "source_location": "### How do I handle split-brain?", "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Two layers: a downing strategy that forces a winner during a partition, and optional leases for the sharding coordinator and singletons. Without a downing strategy the default is 'wait indefinitely' and operators must down nodes by hand."}, {"id": "docs_src_content_docs_reference_faq_journalchoice", "label": "Which journal to use", "file_type": "rationale", "source_file": "docs/src/content/docs/reference/faq.mdx", "source_location": "### What journal should I use?", "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "InMemoryJournal for tests and dev, SqliteJournal for single-node production (best performance-to-simplicity ratio), CassandraJournal when nodes share an event stream, custom otherwise."}, {"id": "docs_src_content_docs_reference_faq_faqprojectionsatleastonce", "label": "Are projections delivered exactly-once?", "file_type": "rationale", "source_file": "docs/src/content/docs/reference/faq.mdx", "source_location": "### Are projections delivered exactly-once?", "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "No - each projection persists its own offset, so a crash between handling event N and persisting offset N re-processes N. Exactly-once needs an idempotent handler (seqNr as dedup key) or a transactional commit of view plus offset."}, {"id": "docs_src_content_docs_reference_faq_typescriptversions", "label": "TypeScript version support", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "docs/src/content/docs/reference/faq.mdx", "source_location": "### What about TypeScript versions?", "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "The framework builds and typechecks with TypeScript 7 (native compiler); published types are consumable from TypeScript 5.6+ (peer range ^5.6 || ^6 || ^7)."}, {"id": "docs_src_content_docs_reference_faq_whytspattern", "label": "Why ts-pattern", "file_type": "rationale", "source_file": "docs/src/content/docs/reference/faq.mdx", "source_location": "### Why ts-pattern?", "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "The cleanest way found to express match().exhaustive() in TS - the discriminated-union dispatch pattern is everywhere in the codebase and a hand-rolled switch loses the exhaustiveness check. Installed automatically alongside actor-ts."}, {"id": "docs_src_content_docs_reference_faq_bunvsnode", "label": "Bun vs Node vs Deno", "file_type": "rationale", "source_file": "docs/src/content/docs/reference/faq.mdx", "source_location": "### Bun vs Node - which should I pick?", "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Bun if you can - faster startup and cold paths, native SQLite and test runner, tested as the primary runtime. Node is fully supported with an identical feature surface; Deno is supported but receives less testing."}, {"id": "docs_src_content_docs_reference_faq_comparisontootherframeworks", "label": "Comparison to JVM / .NET actor toolkits", "file_type": "rationale", "source_file": "docs/src/content/docs/reference/faq.mdx", "source_location": "## Comparison to other actor frameworks", "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "The lineage is real (Akka, Pekko, Orleans) but the differences are: no Scala/JVM, no fiber-based concurrency (JavaScript is single-threaded per process), no streaming DSL, and a smaller surface - a TypeScript-first port of the most useful 80%."}, {"id": "docs_src_content_docs_reference_faq_debuggingnotreceiving", "label": "Why isn't my actor receiving messages", "file_type": "rationale", "source_file": "docs/src/content/docs/reference/faq.mdx", "source_location": "## Debugging", "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Four causes: the ref points at a stopped actor (dead letters), the mailbox is full with reject overflow (MailboxFullError at the sender), recovery has not finished, or recovery FAILED and the actor stopped - the log line to look for is 'recovery failed and onRecoveryFailure returned without rethrowing'."}, {"id": "docs_src_content_docs_reference_faq_debuggingeventsdontreplay", "label": "Why don't my events replay", "file_type": "rationale", "source_file": "docs/src/content/docs/reference/faq.mdx", "source_location": "## Debugging", "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "persistenceId changed between runs, the wrong journal plugin is configured, or the snapshot claims a higher seqNr than the journal and the framework refuses to load it as a corruption guard."}], "edges": [{"source": "docs_src_content_docs_reference_faq_faqpage", "target": "docs_src_content_docs_reference_faq_productionreadiness", "relation": "references", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 1.0, "source_file": "docs/src/content/docs/reference/faq.mdx", "source_location": null, "weight": 1.0}, {"source": "docs_src_content_docs_reference_faq_faqpage", "target": "docs_src_content_docs_reference_faq_whyactorts", "relation": "references", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 1.0, "source_file": "docs/src/content/docs/reference/faq.mdx", "source_location": null, "weight": 1.0}, {"source": "docs_src_content_docs_reference_faq_faqpage", "target": "docs_src_content_docs_reference_faq_nobrowsersupport", "relation": "references", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 1.0, "source_file": "docs/src/content/docs/reference/faq.mdx", "source_location": null, "weight": 1.0}, {"source": "docs_src_content_docs_reference_faq_faqpage", "target": "docs_src_content_docs_reference_faq_tellaskpipeto", "relation": "references", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 1.0, "source_file": "docs/src/content/docs/reference/faq.mdx", "source_location": null, "weight": 1.0}, {"source": "docs_src_content_docs_reference_faq_faqpage", "target": "docs_src_content_docs_reference_faq_persistentvsdurablestate", "relation": "references", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 1.0, "source_file": "docs/src/content/docs/reference/faq.mdx", "source_location": null, "weight": 1.0}, {"source": "d